V. Extraction Guidelines
- Adsorbent information may be scattered across multiple chunks. Combine fields from different chunks only when they clearly describe the same Adsorbent_id.
- If a property field has no extractable value for that record, omit the field. Do not output blank values, null, "not found", or explanatory placeholders. 
- If multiple genuinely different values are reported for the same property, such as when the current study compiles values from different literature sources for the same adsorbent used in the study, retain all reported values as a comma-separated list within the same field. Do not average the values, select a single value, or treat them as experimental replicates. Add `Require_review: Yes` and a concise `Review_reason` indicating that multiple literature-sourced values were reported for the same property.  
- If a candidate adsorbent has no extractable property fields, don't output it as a record. For example, adsorbent name appears in an experimental protocol, performance table, figure caption, comparison statement, or list of tested materials without providing any extractable values for the properties fields should not be output as a record. 
- Evaluate evidence separately for each record and assign a property only when the text unambiguously scopes it to that adsorbent, or to a named adsorbent group whose members are clear from the source chunks and Adsorbent_list.
- Apply the following standardization rules for each component when applicable.
